ssue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122793","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122793.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\nPartially addresses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/14883\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/discussions/15431\r\nBugsquad edit: Addresses regression / problem from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119103\r\n\r\nEDIT since the goal changed: Implements actual glob searching according to https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/core/extensions/file-globbing. If the user search does not include \"/\" or \"*\", the search defaults to using subsequence.\r\n\r\n~Removes the glob searching in the FileSystem, instead using a subsequence search which looks in the file path as well as the file name.~\r\n\r\nNEW video:\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<tr>\r\n <td>\r\n<img width=\"815\" height=\"608\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/529231db-8ff5-4940-9776-160beb6b0aaa\" />\r\n <td>\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/92b9dca0-2788-4518-bc11-80f095448f56\r\n\r\n\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n\r\nOLD video:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c6450fb-6387-45eb-a01e-3e1a50a71271\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nEDIT: Something similar was implemented, see the edit at the top\r\nSince glob search was recently merged in the 4.8 dev cycle, some people may be confused that it doesn't work, so maybe as a fix \"*\" could be replaced with \"\" in these subsequence searches\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122793/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}